// A permit and a forbid for Read. The permit requires a prior
// Login with matching user. The forbid blocks if the user was
// suspended with matching user.
//
// When Suspend's user field is null, the forbid is silenced (the
// join `user: context.input.user` fails against null). The permit still
// evaluates independently and fires. This matches Cedar's
// policy-independence: an error in a forbid does not affect a
// permit.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{ input.user: context.input.user }
};
